WEBVTT

01:50.740 --> 01:53.480
Wow...

01:53.900 --> 01:58.020
The rumors don't do it justice.

01:58.950 --> 02:03.180
Iceland is a harsh land.

02:04.450 --> 02:07.100
There are no trees at all.

02:09.890 --> 02:13.250
The sun's so low in the sky.

02:14.300 --> 02:17.860
I get it now. A land without farms, huh?

02:18.280 --> 02:22.110
You can't grow anything
when the days are so short.

02:22.830 --> 02:24.600
It's winter, after all.

02:25.790 --> 02:29.230
During the summer, the days are long.

02:29.750 --> 02:34.650
Some people grow wheat
where conditions are better,

02:34.650 --> 02:38.610
but it's not nearly enough to fill the
stomachs of the island-dwellers.

02:39.080 --> 02:43.470
Are all the island-dwellers
shepherds and ranchers, then?

02:43.870 --> 02:46.930
No, there are craftsmen and fishermen, too.

02:48.570 --> 02:54.410
There isn't enough pastureland
for everyone to raise livestock,

02:54.410 --> 02:58.370
so some people live
together and fish instead.

02:59.800 --> 03:03.200
Thorfinn's village is one of those.

03:04.460 --> 03:05.820
Huh.

03:06.220 --> 03:09.900
What does that mean? Didn't you live here?

03:10.430 --> 03:14.310
But I was just a child.

03:15.690 --> 03:18.100
I left home when I was
around six years old.

03:18.760 --> 03:24.180
Since then, it's been
a good... uh, at least...

03:25.400 --> 03:28.050
Wait, how old am I?

03:29.410 --> 03:33.580
Thorfinn, Einar,
the village is coming into view.

03:38.190 --> 03:39.450
Whoa...

03:39.450 --> 03:42.670
I suddenly feel scared.

03:42.670 --> 03:45.920
How am I supposed to
face my mother and sister?

03:48.990 --> 03:52.590
You'd better prepare for the worst,
my "prodigal son."

03:54.750 --> 03:57.860
You're finally returning home.

03:55.020 --> 04:01.030
Home.

04:05.680 --> 04:08.240
Okay, that's it.

04:09.870 --> 04:11.370
Good.

04:25.590 --> 04:26.630
There!

04:32.350 --> 04:33.580
Thorfinn...

04:36.800 --> 04:39.500
The villagers are waiting for you.

04:51.420 --> 04:52.200
Who's he?

04:52.200 --> 04:53.650
No idea.

04:53.650 --> 04:55.960
Did Ylva have a little brother?

04:59.450 --> 05:01.860
What's my name, then?

05:01.860 --> 05:02.560
What?

05:02.960 --> 05:06.220
If you used to live here,
then you should know.

05:09.400 --> 05:11.970
F... Faxi?

05:12.280 --> 05:13.400
He got it wrong.

05:13.400 --> 05:14.900
He's suspicious.

05:14.900 --> 05:16.440
Should we tie him up?

05:16.440 --> 05:20.480
No, wait. I can't help it. It's been years.

05:21.710 --> 05:23.220
Mister Leif...

05:25.850 --> 05:29.110
Fine. I guess we'll let him see Ylva.

05:29.110 --> 05:30.990
Yeah.

05:32.540 --> 05:36.540
Ylva's over there, arguing
with the Norwegian merchant.

05:38.850 --> 05:44.880
I warned you not to be
so greedy here, Berge.

05:45.320 --> 05:50.760
S-Sorry, Ylva. I w-won't do it again.

05:50.760 --> 05:54.290
Huh? What was that? I didn't hear you.

05:54.290 --> 05:59.570
Th-That's enough, Ylva.
He returned our money.

05:59.570 --> 06:01.920
Hey, Ylva.

06:04.860 --> 06:08.650
I finally brought him back.

06:09.870 --> 06:11.250
This is Thorfinn.

06:20.300 --> 06:22.300
Thorfinn...

06:24.880 --> 06:26.160
Thorfinn.

06:29.740 --> 06:31.010
Sister.

06:34.670 --> 06:35.720
Sister!

06:39.710 --> 06:42.620
I don't know a Thorfinn!

06:43.480 --> 06:47.760
Come on, Ylva.
It's your little brother, Thorfinn.

06:47.760 --> 06:49.400
Little brother?

06:49.920 --> 06:53.600
Come to think of it,
that might've been his name.

06:53.600 --> 06:56.370
My little brother died when he was a kid.

06:56.370 --> 06:58.640
He's actually alive.

06:58.640 --> 07:01.680
I told you I met him in York before.

07:01.680 --> 07:05.120
Then why didn't you bring him back then?

07:05.120 --> 07:08.460
Well, you know, there was a lot going on...

07:11.690 --> 07:16.100
You made that story up to cheer up
my mother and me, didn't you?

07:16.960 --> 07:18.800
Thank you, Mister Leif.

07:19.740 --> 07:22.480
No, actually...

07:22.870 --> 07:25.060
More importantly...

07:25.060 --> 07:26.360
Huh?

07:26.980 --> 07:32.360
Hey, shorty. You've got some balls
to trick Mister Leif like this.

07:32.360 --> 07:33.360
No, wait!

07:33.360 --> 07:35.920
If you've got something
to say, spit it out.

07:35.920 --> 07:39.140
Man, this has gotten really complicated.

07:40.140 --> 07:44.940
It's surprisingly difficult
to prove who you are.

07:54.310 --> 07:56.870
Let's go to your home, Thorfinn.

07:56.870 --> 07:59.640
Helga will know who you are.

08:00.480 --> 08:02.130
Thorfinn...

08:02.130 --> 08:03.360
Who's that?

08:03.360 --> 08:04.980
He's taking this hard.

08:07.610 --> 08:09.300
I can't blame them.

08:09.810 --> 08:14.200
I'd nearly forgotten the faces
of my sister and mother, too.

08:16.720 --> 08:19.390
It's no surprise they've forgotten me.

08:23.260 --> 08:26.540
Who cares if they have?

08:27.370 --> 08:31.890
You get to see your mother's face
after wandering for over a decade.

08:31.890 --> 08:34.830
If you don't consider yourself lucky,
the gods will smite you.

08:36.140 --> 08:39.240
I was separated from my parents as a kid.

08:39.240 --> 08:42.060
I don't even know where they are now.

08:43.050 --> 08:45.930
I'm jealous of you.

08:49.450 --> 08:53.200
Or shall I go play the devoted son for you?

08:55.610 --> 08:58.080
No. I'm sorry, Bug-Eyes.

08:58.630 --> 08:59.730
Thank you.

09:17.780 --> 09:20.340
Grandma, who's Thorfinn?

09:20.340 --> 09:21.470
Tor-fin...

09:29.020 --> 09:30.240
Thorfinn...

09:31.560 --> 09:32.500
Ma!

09:32.500 --> 09:33.860
What are you doing?

09:33.860 --> 09:36.340
Stop making things more complicated.

09:36.340 --> 09:38.480
Aw, c'mon. Who cares?

09:38.480 --> 09:42.050
No, Helga. This one is...

09:47.840 --> 09:49.470
Thorfinn...

09:52.380 --> 09:53.780
Mother...

09:56.430 --> 10:01.010
You've grown so much.

10:08.540 --> 10:10.750
You look just like him.

10:12.570 --> 10:17.150
You really are your father's son.

10:28.890 --> 10:30.620
Mother...

10:31.710 --> 10:37.330
I'm sorry for everything.

10:40.440 --> 10:44.320
Welcome home, Thorfinn.

11:18.730 --> 11:21.880
Mother, I heard Thorfinn's back.

11:22.210 --> 11:24.400
Welcome back, Dad.

11:24.400 --> 11:25.840
Welcome back.

11:28.640 --> 11:29.950
Thorfinn...

11:37.820 --> 11:39.150
Ari...

11:40.860 --> 11:42.030
Thorfinn.

11:46.170 --> 11:48.850
Thorfinn, I'm sorry.

11:50.270 --> 11:53.920
Because of us, Mister Thors...

12:03.150 --> 12:07.340
Ari, I was an idiot.

12:17.080 --> 12:18.560
Well, then...

12:22.330 --> 12:25.070
Where are you going, Mister Einar?

12:25.360 --> 12:28.570
I should be leaving for the night.

12:28.970 --> 12:33.620
Mister Leif's crew is staying at
the gothi's house. I'll join them there.

12:34.470 --> 12:37.200
You should stay here.

12:37.200 --> 12:40.930
It's a bit cramped,
but we'll figure it out.

12:41.470 --> 12:43.130
But...

12:43.760 --> 12:48.940
If you're Thorfinn's brother,
that makes you my son.

12:44.040 --> 12:45.560
This is my eldest son.

12:45.560 --> 12:47.310
Nice to meet you.

12:47.310 --> 12:48.940
Hello.

12:50.200 --> 12:54.690
This is your home. Don't be shy.

13:01.270 --> 13:07.740
Listen to this, Mother. That stingy
merchant raised the price of salt again.

13:08.780 --> 13:12.920
Hey, it's you again!
How dare you come into our home?

13:12.920 --> 13:15.760
Oh, uh... excuse the intrusion?

13:15.760 --> 13:17.620
Ylva, you haven't heard the—.

13:17.620 --> 13:19.730
Is this an inheritance scam, huh?

13:19.260 --> 13:19.910
What?

13:19.730 --> 13:23.170
Go find a rich family to trick.

13:19.910 --> 13:21.620
Ma's so fast.

13:21.620 --> 13:23.170
And strong.

13:23.960 --> 13:25.720
Ylva, wait.

13:25.720 --> 13:26.420
Huh?

13:27.100 --> 13:31.440
It's really him. Thorfinn's
really come home.

13:31.440 --> 13:33.120
It's really him?

13:33.810 --> 13:37.250
What? I-It can't be.

13:37.250 --> 13:40.960
No way. Mister Leif didn't make it up?

13:43.230 --> 13:45.280
What? Really?

13:48.630 --> 13:51.330
He's the real Thorfinn?

13:52.780 --> 13:55.090
I'm home, Sister.

13:59.920 --> 14:01.170
Thorfinn...

14:01.170 --> 14:02.340
Sister!

14:04.440 --> 14:08.400
Where have you been until now?

14:21.840 --> 14:25.110
Hey... Are you okay, Thorfinn?

14:26.780 --> 14:29.870
I'm fine, Einar.

14:30.570 --> 14:34.240
I'm used to getting hit.

14:43.010 --> 14:43.740
That...

14:44.670 --> 14:46.800
That was just one hit...

14:50.230 --> 14:52.360
Ma's so strong.

14:52.360 --> 14:54.470
You're amazing, Ma.

14:54.470 --> 14:57.220
Ma's the strongest.

15:46.170 --> 15:47.340
That night,

15:48.580 --> 15:56.740
Thorfinn told his family about everything
he'd experienced over the past 16 years.

16:00.010 --> 16:04.920
From Thor's death to his
departure from Ketil's farm.

16:10.840 --> 16:15.760
Though he spoke matter-of-factly
and covered only the key points,

16:15.760 --> 16:18.390
his story of hatred and strife,

16:20.590 --> 16:22.390
death and destruction,

16:25.660 --> 16:27.480
despair and regret,

16:30.860 --> 16:33.740
sadness and rebirth

16:35.240 --> 16:38.590
left everyone who heard
it at a loss for words.

16:48.380 --> 16:50.800
The people I killed,

16:52.350 --> 16:56.630
the slaves who died in despair...

16:58.320 --> 17:03.250
They might've had warm
families like this one.

17:06.890 --> 17:08.850
My sins are heavy.

17:11.800 --> 17:18.400
I have to go to Vinland
to create a peaceful land.

17:24.810 --> 17:26.210
Do it.

17:28.330 --> 17:29.660
Mother...

17:30.290 --> 17:36.380
There are many people who wish
they could flee from this world.

17:37.690 --> 17:45.520
Thors and I fled Jomsborg, the land
of warriors, and came to this island.

17:47.950 --> 17:57.950
For those fleeing from war and slavery,
far beyond the horizon,

17:59.480 --> 18:05.980
you will build a peaceful land where
you'll wait to welcome those people there.

18:09.720 --> 18:16.750
You must live to do that,
Thorfinn, son of Thors.

18:21.420 --> 18:23.790
Thank you, Mother.

18:26.910 --> 18:31.670
So basically, you're going to
establish a country in Vinland?

18:31.670 --> 18:33.770
Sounds like a large-scale endeavor.

18:35.200 --> 18:36.830
He's right.

18:37.830 --> 18:40.370
I can tell you're determined.

18:40.800 --> 18:43.700
But you'll need people,
livestock, materials...

18:44.150 --> 18:46.560
You'll need to buy more boats, too.

18:47.490 --> 18:49.200
It all comes down to money.

18:49.610 --> 18:54.510
It won't be easy pulling together
that much money.

19:00.010 --> 19:03.170
Without my help, that is.

19:06.640 --> 19:09.010
Thank you, Mister Leif.

19:09.560 --> 19:12.120
You're not quitting sailing yet?

19:12.120 --> 19:13.690
I figured you'd say that, Mister Leif.

19:13.690 --> 19:15.800
Will it really be that easy?

19:15.800 --> 19:17.190
They'll be fine.

19:17.190 --> 19:20.070
Don't worry. There are
plenty of ways to do it.

19:20.070 --> 19:23.320
Don't push yourself too hard, Dad.

19:23.320 --> 19:28.110
I'm not pushing myself. You still
don't understand the kind of man I am.

19:48.270 --> 19:53.730
I can't believe you actually went with him.

19:54.940 --> 19:56.220
Sister...

20:00.750 --> 20:01.740
I'm sorry.

20:08.720 --> 20:12.860
Our father was a truly amazing man.

20:13.980 --> 20:16.820
He was strong and kind.

20:17.900 --> 20:22.880
He was looking far ahead
at something I couldn't see.

20:30.560 --> 20:33.580
Well, he was a strange man.

20:57.730 --> 20:59.540
Whose grave is that?

21:00.620 --> 21:04.460
Someone Father once tried to protect.

21:06.410 --> 21:09.510
Were they important?

21:10.860 --> 21:12.350
He was a slave.

21:13.260 --> 21:15.810
He ran away from his master.

21:15.810 --> 21:19.780
My father saved him when
he lay dying on the ground.

21:20.940 --> 21:25.650
My father apparently
traded eight sheep for him.

21:26.000 --> 21:28.080
Eight sheep?

21:32.190 --> 21:36.190
I guess you get your
good nature from your dad.

21:53.180 --> 21:55.750
Man, it's cold.

21:55.750 --> 21:58.890
It's even colder around here at night.

21:58.890 --> 22:01.180
I'm heading back, Thorfinn.

22:13.120 --> 22:14.130
Hey.

22:17.400 --> 22:21.540
Where do the people who
want to run away from here go?

22:28.170 --> 22:31.490
You already know the
answer to that, don't you?
